# Project Operations

Project automation is **plain Python** under `scripts/`. Focused utilities live
under `tools/`. There is no custom orchestrator, Rhai runtime, or Action/Workflow
framework.

Before creating ad-hoc shell one-liners:

1. Prefer an existing script: `python scripts/<name>.py --help`
2. Check focused tools under `./tools/` (`kolibri_img`, `mkfs_utils`,
   `migration_gates`, …)
3. Compose by importing Python functions or calling scripts via `subprocess`

## Architecture

```text
scripts/   = project automation (build, image, QEMU, clean, doctor, …)
tools/     = focused utilities (narrow I/O — not a second orchestrator)
project/   = CONFIG_DATA (e.g. project/build.toml)
```

Do **not** create a monolithic `tools/kolibri_ops` (or similar) that re-hosts
the build/image/QEMU pipeline. Composition belongs in Python scripts; tools stay
focused.

## Agent automation policy

**Python scripts under `scripts/` are the automation boundary used by the AI
agent.**

Do not directly invoke PowerShell, cmd, bash, or one-off shell pipelines for
repository automation when a `scripts/*.py` entry point exists.

```text
python scripts/doctor.py
python scripts/build.py
python scripts/run.py
python scripts/regression.py
python scripts/clean.py
```

Invoke external programs (`cargo`, FASM, QEMU, tool CLIs) from Python via
`subprocess` when extending automation.

If a capability is missing: add or extend a script under `scripts/`, or a focused
tool under `tools/`. Do not introduce a new orchestration framework, DSL, or
Rhai/Lua/JS scripting layer.

## Common commands

```text
python scripts/doctor.py
python scripts/build.py [--mode dev|release] [--skip-tests]
python scripts/prepare_image.py
python scripts/run_qemu.py [--disk exfat] [--disk ntfs] [--headless]
python scripts/run.py
python scripts/regression.py
python scripts/reference_qemu.py
python scripts/mkfs.py [exfat|ntfs] [size]
python scripts/clean.py [--full]
```

## Artifact paths

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `build/` | Production build artifacts |
| `dev_build/` | Disposable test images and temp artifacts |
| `images/` | Persistent FS regression images |
| `project/build.toml` | Blob/migration/image/QEMU CONFIG_DATA |

Do not use `tmp_images/` for new work. See `.cursor/rules/dev-build.mdc`.

## Image handling

See `.cursor/rules/image-handling.mdc` — reference `kolibrios-*.img` is immutable.
